{
  "abstract": "Formalization of a family of pairs of bounded, simply connected, strictly convex planar domains with real-analytic boundaries. At each parameter, the two domains have identical Steklov spectra, including multiplicities. Distinct labels or parameters give noncongruent domains. Each domain has perimeter 2π and no orientation-reversing Euclidean symmetry, and normalized conformal maps converge in C∞ to the identity. The proof uses an explicit degree-seven construction.",
